Several studies have explored the relationship between large-scale hypomethylation and DNA sequence [15, 16]. We sought to explore the extent to which regions with homologous sequence across species shared their PMD state, and in what cases the PMD state was discordant. To do this, we obtained large (50kb or larger) syntenic blocks between human and mouse based on the human–mouse pairwise alignment first reported by [24]. For each of these blocks, we plotted the percentage of the block covered by breast cancer cell line PMDs in human (HCC1954, [7]) vs mouse (4T1, new samples) in Fig. 5A. The marginal distributions show that most blocks are either entirely covered or entirely uncovered by a PMD in both human and mouse. We observed a significant (\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
