Lastly, we sought to understand whether orthologous genes with discordant PMD state had differences in neighborhood gene density, which could indicate past genomic recombination events in one species to a region with different heterochromatin state. To explore this, we calculated the local gene density for each orthologous gene by summing the number of basepairs in its surrounding +/– 100 kb that overlapped with other protein coding genes. We observed directional decreases in gene density: genes overlapped by a mouse PMD but not a human PMD had lower local gene density in mouse than human (\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
